  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 10, 'Workflow A: Registration business process', is a BPMN-style swimlane diagram. The pool is 'Health facility', with lanes Client and Health worker or Clerk. The client arrives at the facility (1), then rapid assessment and management (2) leads to 'Urgent referral necessary?' (3); Yes ends in C. ANC referral. No leads to gather client details (4), then search for client (5) and 'Match found?' (6). No leads to create client record (7); Yes leads to a grouped subprocess 8, Validate client details: review sociodemographic data with the client (8.1), 'Update needed?' (8.2), then update client details (8.3). Both paths reach check-in client (9), ending in B. ANC contact. Fig. 11, 'Notes and annotations for Workflow A: Registration business process', is a three-column text panel that annotates each numbered activity of Fig. 10 — for example, that rapid assessment is outside the DAK's scope, and the identifiers a client may present when searched for. Both cite WHO (29).",
